Cintai is a focused combat meditation that sharpens the monk's awareness
of their opponent's movements and vulnerabilities. Through this heightened
concentration, the monk anticipates defensive reactions and identifies
openings that others would miss.

This passive skill provides a significant bonus to the monk's chance to
hit opponents with bare-handed attacks. At maximum mastery, cintai adds
up to +15 to the monk's attack bonus, representing the cumulative advantage
of superior focus and timing.

The technique requires no activation and functions automatically in combat.
The bonus applies to all bare-handed strikes, making the monk progressively
more accurate as their mastery of cintai deepens. Combined with the monk's
natural speed and multiple attacks, cintai ensures that a skilled monk
rarely wastes a strike.

